                                                "sense_id": "849118d4-7724-3c3c-a7ed-57feff1a3044",
                                                "text": "In colonial times, when land was not worth much and banks didn’t exist, most lending was based on human property. In the early 1700s, slaves were the dominant collateral in South Carolina."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f255574f-e468-32a2-9c8a-64f9e89b088f",
